`GRAPH_REGISTRY` is keyed by graph **name only**, with no Redis logical-database qualifier. Using the same graph key name in two databases (`SELECT 0` / `SELECT 1`) makes the second registration displace the first. On a debug build this trips a `debug_assert!` and, via the module's panic hook, **kills the whole Redis process**. On a release build there is no panic, but the first graph is silently evicted from the registry and becomes **permanently write-locked** — every subsequent write aborts, and the state is unrecoverable without destroying the data.

Two ordinary commands from an ordinary client are enough.

