**Short reads inside a `graphmeta` key still segfault**

`_GraphMetaType_RdbLoad` (`src/serializers/graphmeta_type.c:41`) registers the result of `RdbLoadGraph` without the NULL check this PR adds to `graphcontext_type.c`. Since `RdbLoadGraph` now returns NULL on a short read, a truncation inside any graphmeta key ends in `Globals_AddGraph(NULL)` → `GraphContext_IncreaseRefCount` → SIGSEGV.

Reproduced with this PR's CI build (38a53b9, linux arm64) on a 260k-node graph stored in 4 keys, cutting `dump.rdb` at 10 points: 9 segfault (exit 139); only the cut inside the `graphdata` key exits cleanly. A diskless full sync (`repl-diskless-load flushdb`) that loses its connection mid-transfer crashes the same way.

`test_short_read` truncates a `DUMP` payload, which is a single graphdata value, so it never reaches the graphmeta loader. Suggested fix, mirroring `graphcontext_type.c`:
```c
if(gc == NULL) {
	return NULL;
}
GraphContext_RegisterWithModule(gc);
```

